IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`

-- Employment Insurance Regulations (SOR/96-332), Part IV: Pilot Project No. 1 (reg 77, periodic claims) and Pilot Project No. 5 (reg 77.1, choosing not to be paid).
-- Piece er5, LAYER 1: the law, objectively. Every `src:N` is a line of SOR-96-332.txt. The text is an unofficial rendering;
-- nothing here is claimed to be verified against the official text.
--
-- Both pilot projects are spent: Pilot Project No. 1 covered periods of eligibility from June 30, 1996 to June 26, 1999, and reg 77.1 gives no dates at all
-- ("the week in which this section comes into force" and "ceases to have effect" are not stated in the text). They are encoded in full, with every date a
-- plain input, so that each rule answers correctly for the claimant it governed (see NOTES.md, "What the text does not answer").
--
-- Relations (Hohfeld): reg 77(5) gives a participant a deemed claim (a power, with the Commission subject to it); reg 77(6) gives the Commission the power to
-- end participation (the participant is liable to it); reg 77(4)(b) puts a duty on the participant to tell the Commission; reg 77.1(3) and (5) give the claimant a
-- power to choose, and to rescind the choice; reg 77.1(4)(b) puts a liability on the claimant to repay.

§ `Regulations Part IV - Pilot Projects`

§§ `Reg 77(1) - Pilot Project No. 1: purpose`

-- src:1397 | 77 (1) The Commission shall establish Pilot Project No. 1 for the purpose of assessing the cost, the validity of payment, the operational impact and the effect on customer service to claimants of exempting them from the requirement in sections 49 and 50 of the Act to make periodic claims for benefits.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 77(1) (src:1397)
`reg 77(1) the purpose of Pilot Project No. 1` MEANS
    "assessing the cost, the validity of payment, the operational impact and the effect on customer service to claimants of exempting them from the requirement in sections 49 and 50 of the Act to make periodic claims for benefits"

§§ `Reg 77(2) - definitions`

-- "condition of entitlement to benefits means any requirement, circumstance or condition referred to in subsection 49(1) of the Act."
-- src:1399 | condition of entitlement to benefits means any requirement, circumstance or condition referred to in subsection 49(1) of the Act. (condition d'admissibilité au bénéfice des prestations)
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 77(2) "condition of entitlement to benefits" (src:1399)
GIVEN `the requirement, circumstance or condition is one referred to in subsection 49(1) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: s 49(1) of the Act (piece ei2)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 77(2) condition of entitlement to benefits` IF
    `the requirement, circumstance or condition is one referred to in subsection 49(1) of the Act`

-- "period of eligibility" for the benefits of (3)(d)(i) (pregnancy, or caring for a new-born or adopted child) is the aggregate of the waiting period and the period of s 22(2)
-- (with any extension), or of the period of s 23(2) and the waiting period, "unless that waiting period has already been taken into account" for the first.
-- Only where the period begins and where it ends matter to the pilot project, so the aggregate is carried as the period from the earliest first day to the latest last day of
-- the periods that apply; the waiting period counts once however many benefits are claimed. Reading taken (fork F-reg77a): (i) is the pregnancy benefits of s 22 and
-- (ii) the benefits of s 23 for a new-born or adopted child, and a claimant of both has both.
-- src:1400 | period of eligibility means
-- src:1401 | (a) in respect of the benefits referred to in subparagraph (3) (d) (i)
-- src:1402 | (i) the aggregate of the waiting period referred to in section 13 of the Act and the period described in subsection 22(2) of the Act and any extension of the period described in subsection 22(2) of the Act, or
-- src:1403 | (ii) the aggregate of the period referred to in subsection 23(2) of the Act and the waiting period referred to in section 13 of the Act, unless that waiting period has already been taken into account for the purposes of subparagraph (i); and
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 77(2) "period of eligibility" (a) (src:1400-1403)
GIVEN `the waiting period referred to in section 13 of the Act` IS A `Period of days` -- out of range: s 13 of the Act (piece ei1)
      `the claimant claims benefits for pregnancy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the period described in subsection 22(2) of the Act, with any extension of it` IS A `Period of days` -- out of range: s 22(2) of the Act (piece ei1)
      `the claimant claims benefits for caring for a new-born or adopted child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the period referred to in subsection 23(2) of the Act` IS A `Period of days` -- out of range: s 23(2) of the Act (piece ei1)
GIVETH A MAYBE `Period of days`
DECIDE `reg 77(2) the period of eligibility for the benefits referred to in subparagraph 77(3)(d)(i)` IS
    IF NOT (`the claimant claims benefits for pregnancy` OR `the claimant claims benefits for caring for a new-born or adopted child`)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (`Period of days` OF
                   (Date (minimum (map (GIVEN p YIELD `er5 reg 77 the day number of the first day of` p) `the periods that apply`))),
                   (Date (maximum (map (GIVEN p YIELD `er5 reg 77 the day number of the last day of` p) `the periods that apply`))))
    WHERE
        `the periods that apply` MEANS
            `the waiting period referred to in section 13 of the Act` FOLLOWED BY
                (append (IF `the claimant claims benefits for pregnancy` THEN LIST `the period described in subsection 22(2) of the Act, with any extension of it` ELSE EMPTY)
                        (IF `the claimant claims benefits for caring for a new-born or adopted child` THEN LIST `the period referred to in subsection 23(2) of the Act` ELSE EMPTY))

GIVEN p IS A `Period of days`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `er5 reg 77 the day number of the first day of` IS Day (p's `first day of the period`)

GIVEN p IS A `Period of days`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `er5 reg 77 the day number of the last day of` IS Day (p's `last day of the period`)

-- (b) for the benefits of (3)(d)(ii), "the period during which the claimant attends a course or program, referred to in paragraph 25(1)(a) of the Act, that is an apprenticeship course or an apprenticeship program".
-- src:1404 | (b) in respect of the benefits referred to in subparagraph (3)(d)(ii), the period during which the claimant attends a course or program, referred to in paragraph 25(1)(a) of the Act, that is an apprenticeship course or an apprenticeship program. (période d'admissibilité)
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 77(2) "period of eligibility" (b) (src:1404)
GIVEN `the period during which the claimant attends a course or program referred to in paragraph 25(1)(a) of the Act` IS A `Period of days` -- out of range: s 25(1)(a) of the Act (piece ei2)
      `that course or program is an apprenticeship course or an apprenticeship program` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Period of days`
DECIDE `reg 77(2) the period of eligibility for the benefits referred to in subparagraph 77(3)(d)(ii)` IS
    IF `that course or program is an apprenticeship course or an apprenticeship program`
    THEN JUST `the period during which the claimant attends a course or program referred to in paragraph 25(1)(a) of the Act`
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Reg 77(3) and (7) - eligibility to participate`

-- (7) Paragraph (3)(a) ceases to be in force on April 1, 1997: the residence condition is part of the test only before that day. Which day the test is taken on is not said (fork F-reg77b).
-- src:1417 | (7) Paragraph (3)(a) ceases to be in force on April 1, 1997.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 77(7) (src:1417)
GIVEN `the day on which the claimant's eligibility is tested` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 77(7) paragraph 77(3)(a) is in force on the day` IF
    `the day on which the claimant's eligibility is tested` BELOW (YMD 1997 4 1)

-- (3) A claimant is eligible to participate where (a) the claimant resides in Canada; (b) the claimant makes an initial claim for benefits or a claim in respect of which s 26(2) applies;
-- (c) the claimant's period of eligibility begins on or after June 30, 1996 and ends not later than June 26, 1999; and (d) the claimant makes a claim for benefits in respect of every
-- week of unemployment in the period of eligibility (i) for either of the reasons in paragraphs 12(3)(a) and (b), or (ii) under section 25, to attend an apprenticeship course or program.
-- (d) is carried as one fact: every such week is claimed, each for one or the other reason.
-- src:1405 | (3) A claimant is eligible to participate in Pilot Project No. 1 where
-- src:1406 | (a) the claimant resides in Canada;
-- src:1407 | (b) the claimant makes an initial claim for benefits or a claim in respect of which subsection 26(2) applies;
-- src:1408 | (c) the claimant's period of eligibility begins on or after June 30, 1996 and ends not later than June 26, 1999; and
-- src:1409 | (d) the claimant makes a claim for benefits in respect of every week of unemployment in the claimant's period of eligibility
-- src:1410 | (i) for either of the reasons referred to in paragraphs 12(3)(a) and (b) of the Act, or
-- src:1411 | (ii) under section 25 of the Act, to attend an apprenticeship course or an apprenticeship program.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 77(3) (src:1405-1411)
GIVEN `the claimant resides in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the claimant's eligibility is tested` IS A DATE
      `the claimant makes an initial claim for benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant makes a claim in respect of which subsection 26(2) of the Act applies` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: s 26(2) of the Act (piece ei2)
      `the claimant's period of eligibility` IS A `Period of days`
      `the claimant makes a claim for benefits in respect of every week of unemployment in the period of eligibility, each either for a reason referred to in paragraphs 12(3)(a) and (b) of the Act or under section 25 of the Act to attend an apprenticeship course or an apprenticeship program` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 77(3) the claimant is eligible to participate in Pilot Project No. 1` IF
        ((NOT (`reg 77(7) paragraph 77(3)(a) is in force on the day` `the day on which the claimant's eligibility is tested`)) OR `the claimant resides in Canada`)
    AND (`the claimant makes an initial claim for benefits` OR `the claimant makes a claim in respect of which subsection 26(2) of the Act applies`)
    AND (`the claimant's period of eligibility`'s `first day of the period`) AT LEAST (YMD 1996 6 30)
    AND (`the claimant's period of eligibility`'s `last day of the period`) AT MOST (YMD 1999 6 26)
    AND `the claimant makes a claim for benefits in respect of every week of unemployment in the period of eligibility, each either for a reason referred to in paragraphs 12(3)(a) and (b) of the Act or under section 25 of the Act to attend an apprenticeship course or an apprenticeship program`

§§ `Reg 77(4) - the form`

-- A claimant who is eligible and wishes to participate shall complete and sign a form, supplied by the Commission, agreeing that (a) to the best of the claimant's knowledge at the time of signing, no condition of entitlement
-- will go unmet for any week of the period of eligibility after the waiting period (except earnings deductible under s 19, 22 or 23 of the Act); and (b) the claimant will notify the Commission of a condition they cease to meet.
-- The text does not say in so many words that signing makes a claimant a participant; it is read so, since (5) speaks of "a claimant who participates" (fork F-reg77c).
-- src:1412 | (4) A claimant who is eligible to participate in Pilot Project No. 1 and who wishes to participate in the project shall complete and sign a form, supplied by the Commission, agreeing that
-- src:1413 | (a) to the best of the claimant's knowledge at the time of signing the form, there are no conditions of entitlement to benefits that will not be fully met for each week in the period of eligibility following the waiting period, except in respect of earnings that may be deducted pursuant to section 19, 22 or 23 of the Act during that period; and
-- src:1414 | (b) should the claimant cease to meet a condition of entitlement to benefits at any time during the period of eligibility where failure to meet that condition has the effect of reducing or eliminating any benefits for any week in the period of eligibility, the claimant will notify the Commission of the condition as soon as possible.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 77(4) (src:1412-1414)
GIVEN `the claimant has completed and signed the form supplied by the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the form records the claimant's agreement that, to the best of their knowledge at the time of signing, there are no conditions of entitlement to benefits that will not be fully met for each week in the period of eligibility following the waiting period, except in respect of earnings that may be deducted under section 19, 22 or 23 of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the form records the claimant's agreement to notify the Commission as soon as possible if they cease to meet a condition of entitlement to benefits during the period of eligibility where failure to meet it has the effect of reducing or eliminating benefits for any week` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 77(4) the claimant has signed the form with the agreements it requires` IF
        `the claimant has completed and signed the form supplied by the Commission`
    AND `the form records the claimant's agreement that, to the best of their knowledge at the time of signing, there are no conditions of entitlement to benefits that will not be fully met for each week in the period of eligibility following the waiting period, except in respect of earnings that may be deducted under section 19, 22 or 23 of the Act`
    AND `the form records the claimant's agreement to notify the Commission as soon as possible if they cease to meet a condition of entitlement to benefits during the period of eligibility where failure to meet it has the effect of reducing or eliminating benefits for any week`

-- src:1412 | (4) A claimant who is eligible to participate in Pilot Project No. 1 and who wishes to participate in the project shall complete and sign a form, supplied by the Commission, agreeing that
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 77(4) (src:1412)
GIVEN `the claimant is eligible to participate in Pilot Project No. 1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant wishes to participate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant has signed the form with the agreements it requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 77(4) the claimant participates in Pilot Project No. 1` IF
        `the claimant is eligible to participate in Pilot Project No. 1`
    AND `the claimant wishes to participate`
    AND `the claimant has signed the form with the agreements it requires`

-- (b) "should the claimant cease to meet a condition of entitlement to benefits at any time during the period of eligibility where failure to meet that condition has the effect of reducing
-- or eliminating any benefits for any week in the period of eligibility, the claimant will notify the Commission of the condition as soon as possible." No number of days is given.
-- src:1414 | (b) should the claimant cease to meet a condition of entitlement to benefits at any time during the period of eligibility where failure to meet that condition has the effect of reducing or eliminating any benefits for any week in the period of eligibility, the claimant will notify the Commission of the condition as soon as possible.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 77(4)(b) (src:1414)
GIVEN `the claimant participates in Pilot Project No. 1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant ceases to meet a condition of entitlement to benefits at some time during the period of eligibility` IS A BOOLEAN
      `failure to meet that condition has the effect of reducing or eliminating benefits for a week in the period of eligibility` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 77(4)(b) the claimant must notify the Commission of the condition as soon as possible` IF
        `the claimant participates in Pilot Project No. 1`
    AND `the claimant ceases to meet a condition of entitlement to benefits at some time during the period of eligibility`
    AND `failure to meet that condition has the effect of reducing or eliminating benefits for a week in the period of eligibility`

§§ `Reg 77(5) - deemed claims`

-- For the purposes of sections 49 and 50 of the Act, a claimant who participates is deemed to have made a claim for benefits for every week of unemployment in the period of eligibility.
-- A week is in the period when all seven of its days are.
-- src:1415 | (5) For the purposes of sections 49 and 50 of the Act, a claimant who participates in Pilot Project No. 1 is, for the purpose of this section, deemed to have made a claim for benefits for every week of unemployment in the claimant's period of eligibility.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 77(5) (src:1415)
GIVEN `the claimant participates in Pilot Project No. 1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Sunday that begins the week` IS A DATE
      `the week is a week of unemployment` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: s 11 of the Act (piece ei1)
      `the claimant's period of eligibility` IS A `Period of days`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 77(5) the claimant is deemed to have made a claim for benefits for the week` IF
        `the claimant participates in Pilot Project No. 1`
    AND `the week is a week of unemployment`
    AND `the Sunday that begins the week` AT LEAST (`the claimant's period of eligibility`'s `first day of the period`)
    AND (`the Sunday that begins the week` PLUS 6) AT MOST (`the claimant's period of eligibility`'s `last day of the period`)

§§ `Reg 77(6) - the Commission may end participation`

-- Where the Commission becomes aware that the claimant does not meet a condition of entitlement during the period of eligibility, it may terminate the claimant's participation as of the date on which it
-- becomes aware. The Commission's choice to terminate is a BOOLEAN input; without both the awareness and the choice there is no date (NOTHING).
-- src:1416 | (6) Where the Commission becomes aware that the claimant does not meet a condition of entitlement to benefits during the claimant's period of eligibility, the Commission may terminate the claimant's participation in Pilot Project No. 1 as of the date on which the Commission becomes aware of the claimant's failure to meet the condition.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 77(6) (src:1416)
GIVEN `the Commission becomes aware that the claimant does not meet a condition of entitlement to benefits during the period of eligibility` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission decides to terminate the claimant's participation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the Commission becomes aware` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `reg 77(6) the day as of which the claimant's participation is terminated` IS
    IF     `the Commission becomes aware that the claimant does not meet a condition of entitlement to benefits during the period of eligibility`
       AND `the Commission decides to terminate the claimant's participation`
    THEN JUST `the day on which the Commission becomes aware`
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Reg 77.1(1) - Pilot Project No. 5: purpose`

-- src:1420 | 77.1 (1) The Commission establishes Pilot Project No. 5 for the purpose of assessing the effect of allowing claimants who are entitled to benefits for one or more weeks for which they receive or are entitled to receive an indemnity payment described in paragraph 35(2)(f) to choose not to be paid benefits for those weeks.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 77.1(1) (src:1420)
`reg 77.1(1) the purpose of Pilot Project No. 5` MEANS
    "assessing the effect of allowing claimants who are entitled to benefits for one or more weeks for which they receive or are entitled to receive an indemnity payment described in paragraph 35(2)(f) to choose not to be paid benefits for those weeks"

§§ `Reg 77.1(2) and (6) - who is included, and the weeks`

-- Neither the day on which reg 77.1 comes into force nor the day on which it ceases to have effect is stated in the text: both are inputs. "The Pilot Project" is read as the time from the first to the second.
-- (6) The pilot project does not apply to a week preceding the week in which the section comes into force or a week following the week in which it ceases to have effect.
-- src:1430 | (6) Pilot Project No. 5 does not apply to a week preceding the week in which this section comes into force or a week following the week in which this section ceases to have effect.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 77.1(6) (src:1430)
GIVEN `the Sunday that begins the week` IS A DATE
      `the day on which this section comes into force` IS A DATE -- the text does not state it
      `the day on which this section ceases to have effect` IS A DATE -- the text does not state it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 77.1(6) Pilot Project No. 5 applies to the week` IF
        `the Sunday that begins the week` AT LEAST (`s 2(1) the Sunday that begins the week containing` `the day on which this section comes into force`)
    AND `the Sunday that begins the week` AT MOST (`s 2(1) the Sunday that begins the week containing` `the day on which this section ceases to have effect`)

-- (2) Pilot Project No. 5 includes all claimants (a) whose benefit period begins or ends during the Pilot Project; (b) who receive or are entitled to receive an indemnity payment described in paragraph 35(2)(f)
-- during their benefit period; and (c) who are entitled to benefits for one or more weeks for which they receive or are entitled to receive that payment.
-- src:1421 | (2) Pilot Project No. 5 includes all claimants
-- src:1422 | (a) whose benefit period begins or ends during the Pilot Project;
-- src:1423 | (b) who receive or are entitled to receive an indemnity payment described in paragraph 35(2)(f) during their benefit period; and
-- src:1424 | (c) who are entitled to benefits for one or more weeks for which they receive or are entitled to receive an indemnity payment described in paragraph 35(2)(f).
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 77.1(2) (src:1421-1424)
GIVEN `the day on which the claimant's benefit period begins` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the claimant's benefit period ends, if it has` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day on which this section comes into force` IS A DATE -- the text does not state it
      `the day on which this section ceases to have effect` IS A DATE -- the text does not state it
      `the claimant receives or is entitled to receive an indemnity payment described in paragraph 35(2)(f) during the benefit period` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: reg 35(2)(f) (piece er3)
      `the claimant is entitled to benefits for one or more weeks for which they receive or are entitled to receive that payment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 77.1(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 5` IF
        (   `the day` `the day on which the claimant's benefit period begins` `falls within` (`Period of days` OF `the day on which this section comes into force`, `the day on which this section ceases to have effect`)
         OR (CONSIDER `the day on which the claimant's benefit period ends, if it has`
             WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
             WHEN JUST ends THEN `the day` ends `falls within` (`Period of days` OF `the day on which this section comes into force`, `the day on which this section ceases to have effect`)))
    AND `the claimant receives or is entitled to receive an indemnity payment described in paragraph 35(2)(f) during the benefit period`
    AND `the claimant is entitled to benefits for one or more weeks for which they receive or are entitled to receive that payment`

§§ `Reg 77.1(3) to (5) - choosing not to be paid`

-- (3) A claimant who chooses not to be paid benefits to which they are entitled for such weeks is, for the purposes of paragraph 10(10)(d) of the Act, deemed to have proved that they are not entitled to benefits for those weeks.
-- (4) For a claimant who chooses not to be paid after being paid for such weeks: (a) if the Commission informed the claimant about the project before they were paid, (3) does not apply to the weeks paid;
-- (b) if it did not, (3) applies to those weeks and the claimant must repay the benefits paid. (5) A claimant may rescind a choice made under (3); a claimant who rescinds shall be paid benefits to which they are entitled.
-- A choice that has been rescinded no longer has its effect under (3) or (4)(b) (fork F-reg77.1).
-- src:1425 | (3) A claimant who chooses not to be paid benefits to which they are entitled for one or more weeks for which they receive or are entitled to receive an indemnity payment described in paragraph 35(2)(f) is, for the purposes of paragraph 10(10)(d) of the Act, deemed to have proved that they are not entitled to benefits for those weeks.
-- src:1426 | (4) The following applies to a claimant who, after being paid benefits for one or more weeks for which they received or were entitled to receive an indemnity payment described in paragraph 35(2)(f), chooses not to be paid benefits:
-- src:1427 | (a) if the Commission informed the claimant about Pilot Project No. 5 before the claimant was paid benefits, subsection (3) does not apply in respect of the week or weeks for which a benefit was paid; and
-- src:1428 | (b) if the Commission did not inform the claimant about the Pilot Project before the claimant was paid benefits, subsection (3) applies in respect of the week or weeks for which a benefit was paid and the claimant must repay the benefits paid.
-- src:1429 | (5) A claimant may rescind a choice made by them under subsection (3). A claimant who rescinds shall be paid benefits to which they are entitled.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 77.1(3), reg 77.1(4), reg 77.1(5) (src:1425-1429)
GIVEN `the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 5` IS A BOOLEAN
      `Pilot Project No. 5 applies to the week` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant chooses not to be paid benefits to which they are entitled for the week` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant makes that choice after being paid benefits for the week` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission informed the claimant about Pilot Project No. 5 before the claimant was paid benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant has rescinded the choice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 77.1(3) the claimant is deemed to have proved that they are not entitled to benefits for the week` IF
        `the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 5`
    AND `Pilot Project No. 5 applies to the week`
    AND `the claimant chooses not to be paid benefits to which they are entitled for the week`
    AND (NOT `the claimant has rescinded the choice`)
    AND (   (NOT `the claimant makes that choice after being paid benefits for the week`)
         OR (NOT `the Commission informed the claimant about Pilot Project No. 5 before the claimant was paid benefits`))

-- src:1428 | (b) if the Commission did not inform the claimant about the Pilot Project before the claimant was paid benefits, subsection (3) applies in respect of the week or weeks for which a benefit was paid and the claimant must repay the benefits paid.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 77.1(4)(b) (src:1428)
GIVEN `the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 5` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant chooses not to be paid benefits after being paid benefits for the week` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission informed the claimant about Pilot Project No. 5 before the claimant was paid benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant has rescinded the choice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 77.1(4)(b) the claimant must repay the benefits paid for the week` IF
        `the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 5`
    AND `the claimant chooses not to be paid benefits after being paid benefits for the week`
    AND (NOT `the Commission informed the claimant about Pilot Project No. 5 before the claimant was paid benefits`)
    AND (NOT `the claimant has rescinded the choice`)

-- src:1429 | (5) A claimant may rescind a choice made by them under subsection (3). A claimant who rescinds shall be paid benefits to which they are entitled.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 77.1(5) (src:1429)
GIVEN `the claimant made a choice under subsection 77.1(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant rescinds the choice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 77.1(5) the claimant is to be paid the benefits to which they are entitled` IF
        `the claimant made a choice under subsection 77.1(3)`
    AND `the claimant rescinds the choice`
